en by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{4\\pi }{5}=\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{(\\frac{4\\pi }{5})}=\\frac{5}{4}.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the tangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $\\frac{1}{2}$ unit up. Hence, $D=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, $B+D=\\frac{5}{4}+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{7}{4}.$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{5x}{4})+\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398172 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398173 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398172 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398174 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398172 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398175 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398172 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398176 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398172 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398177 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398172 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398172 1077 "selection" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398172 1079 #edb/ref 17592186398174 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398172 1080 #uuid "b20222d5-4d8b-5ef3-b5e6-cdd257fd9b17" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398173 1081 "\\frac{7}{2}" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398173 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398173 1084 #uuid "34eca68d-7384-5ac4-aae3-9fd3ad9100c9" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398174 1081 "\\frac{7}{4}" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398174 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398174 1084 #uuid "ebf81549-b73c-5aa8-ae6f-2eb529e3d650" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398175 1081 "\\frac{5}{2}" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398175 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398175 1084 #uuid "4b365ba9-edc9-5d4f-9d0c-a4e1280cad8f" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398176 1081 "3" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398176 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398176 1084 #uuid "95065041-df6a-55e2-ba59-eb39e1ef3c42" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398177 1081 "4" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398177 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398177 1084 #uuid "4041d9b8-a50e-5114-a489-9911977efeb5" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398178 1068 #edb/ref 17592186398179 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398178 1069 "q-117799" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398178 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398178 1071 "![](images/c9/c9ed24a7fa07d6c29e4125c8428fb61a42fc969b99f101c4737bdedf9bf036ff.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx)+D,$ where $B$ and $D$ are constants. What is $B+D?$" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398178 1072 #uuid "554b2923-f03c-51dd-9817-6e0a2f8280b5" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398178 1074 "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{4\\pi }{3}-0=\\frac{4\\pi }{3}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{4\\pi }{3}=\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{(\\frac{4\\pi }{3})}=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the cotangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $3$ units down. Hence, $D=-3.$\n\nTherefore, $B+D=\\frac{3}{4}+(-3)=-\\frac{9}{4}.$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{3x}{4})-3.\n$$" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398179 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398180 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398179 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398181 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398179 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398182 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398179 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398183 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398179 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398184 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398179 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398179 1077 "selection" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398179 1079 #edb/ref 17592186398182 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398179 1080 #uuid "4b387afd-4a67-578b-8db3-0662089f213d" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398180 1081 "-\\frac{5}{2}" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398180 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398180 1084 #uuid "dd86b80a-f69a-5bee-9e25-9498124a3b56" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398181 1081 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398181 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398181 1084 #uuid "ae4cbf13-3436-5ca9-a85e-d79666e97f91" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398182 1081 "-\\frac{9}{4}" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398182 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398182 1084 #uuid "a192845d-5444-593f-a294-b8369a05e099" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398183 1081 "2" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398183 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398183 1084 #uuid "e570139b-a17c-5e71-8fdc-ac883bda1ab2" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398184 1081 "-1" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398184 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398184 1084 #uuid "c337dc59-1dd1-5197-98b9-3c6fcbf08e62" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398185 1068 #edb/ref 17592186398186 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398185 1069 "q-117969" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398185 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398185 1071 "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=x(y-1),\\,y(1)=1\n$$\n\nUse Euler's method with three steps of equal size to approximate $y(4).$" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398185 1072 #uuid "0f77be12-c79a-5d32-a315-5527f2d659be" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398185 1074 "First, note that we are given $y(1)$ and asked to find $y(4).$ The distance from $x=1$ and $x=4$ is $3,$ and since we are asked to use three steps of equal size, our step size must be\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{4-1}{3}=\\frac{3}{3}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with Euler's method. We'll start by creating a table that includes the initial condition data $y(1)=1.$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n**Step 1.** We compute ${y}^{′}$ and $Δy$ (using the values of $x$ and $y$ in the first row) and the values of ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =x(y-1)=1\\cdot (1-1)=0 \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=0\\cdot 1=0 \\\\ {x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=1+1=2 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=1+0=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $2$ | $1$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n**Step 2.** We compute ${y}^{′}$ and $Δy$ (using the values of $x$ and $y$ in the second row) and new values of ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =x(y-1)=2\\cdot (1-1)=0 \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=0\\cdot 1=0 \\\\ {x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=2+1=3 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=1+0=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $2$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $3$ | $1$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n**Step 3.** We compute ${y}^{′}$ and $Δy$ (using the values of $x$ and $y$ in the third row) and new values of ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =x(y-1)=3\\cdot (1-1)=0 \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=0\\cdot 1=0 \\\\ {x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=3+1=4 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=1+0=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table. \n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $2$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $3$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $4$ | $1$ |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(4)≈1.$" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398186 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398187 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398186 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398188 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398186 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398189 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398186 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398190 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398186 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398191 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398186 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398186 1077 "selection" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398186 1079 #edb/ref 17592186398189 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398186 1080 #uuid "63a67a32-debb-51c3-9081-1309e01431cc" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398187 1081 "3" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398187 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398187 1084 #uuid "743abfee-b36a-5b90-a068-6de3e3d0e361" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398188 1081 "2" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398188 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398188 1084 #uuid "c549a040-b264-5669-b784-47b0d206e0bf" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398189 1081 "1" 13194139533473 17592186045585 true] [17592186398189 1083 #edb/ref 1759218604549